        <h2 class="section-headline section-headline--light reveal">Where does direct conversion matter most?</h2>
        <ul class="tech-list tech-list--grid reveal">
          <li><strong>Intraoral dental imaging</strong> — sharpness and contrast at low dose in a compact sensor.</li>
          <li><strong>Panoramic &amp; cephalometric imaging</strong> — scanning geometry with high sensitivity across the exposure.</li>
          <li><strong>Industrial inline inspection</strong> — high line rates with enough contrast to catch small defects and contaminants.</li>
          <li><strong>Food &amp; beverage inspection</strong> — foreign-object detection where subtle density differences matter.</li>
          <li><strong>Electronics inspection</strong> — fine-pitch PCB, component and solder-joint detail.</li>
          <li><strong>Medical imaging</strong> — dose efficiency and contrast resolution in scanning modalities.</li>
          <li><strong>Custom OEM systems</strong> — the modular UFS platform scales from 7.5 cm to 12 m of active length.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="tech-body tech-body--dark reveal">
          See <a href="/applications.html">Applications</a> for the full overview of dental, medical and industrial use cases.
        </p>
